	The Plane of Air is always lousy with dragons. You should have
resistances against most of their attacks, but you probably don't have
acid resistance, if you've been a good little monk, you won't have
disintegration resistance, and shock resistance is not enough to keep
blue dragons from destroying your rings and wands... and losing your
levitation source on the Plane of Air will pretty well screw you.

	If you really feel you need life saving, wish for the shield of
reflection. Me, I just make sure I've got plenty of hit points and a few
potions of full healing where I can get to them quick and go without
life saving, if the alternative is going without reflection or going
without two-weapon and/or spellcasting. This strategy's worked for me
every time so far.

